\Rightarrow \quad f($\mathrm{l})=$ f(x)-1-x+2\{\because f(0)=1\}
\end{gathered} On differentiating with respect to ' $ x$ ' 0=$\frac{d f(x)}{d x}-0-1+0 \Rightarrow \quad \frac{d f(x)}{d x}=1 So, \frac{d f(x)}{d x}($ at $x=e)=1$

